storytold-effectcraft (0.25.1-1~smallgearlab1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging of EffectCraft 0.25.1, an open-source a motion graphics and compositing editor
    written in Rust (storytold/effectcraft), from the upstream release tag.
  * Built offline with the local rustup toolchain from the crates that
    build.sh vendored. The default features are built, as upstream's own deb
    build does.
  * Two packages, split as storytold-vectorcraft is: storytold-effectcraft (the
    editor window) and storytold-effectcraft-cli (the headless renderer, command runner and MCP server). The packages carry
    the storytold prefix of their upstream organisation; the programs keep
    their names (/usr/bin/effectcraft, /usr/bin/effectcraft-cli). The CLI has no
    windowing or GPU dependencies; the editor recommends it. Both depend on
    ALSA (loaded at run time), as upstream's nfpm.yaml lists.
  * The CLI has no man page generator or shell completions upstream, so the
    man pages are written here (debian/effectcraft.1, debian/effectcraft-cli.1).
  * debian/copyright: gen-crate-licenses.py writes a paragraph for each Rust
    crate that is linked in, and the .docs files install the license files of
    those crates and of the bundled fonts.

 -- small-gear-lab <289302950+marie-222@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:30:00 +0900
